    "result_text": "Done. The change is complete and the test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`).\n\n## What I did\n\nThe spec required moving date-derived values onto a fiscal-year basis (fiscal year starts 1 July), exposing a new `fiscalYear` field as `FY<YY>`, and changing two existing behaviours. I made the fiscal-year rule a single source of truth so every consumer agrees.\n\n**New `mapper/FiscalYear.java`** \u2014 derives fiscal-year values from a date. The fiscal year runs 1 July\u201330 June and is identified by the calendar year it *ends* (standard FY notation, e.g. 1 Jul 2025\u201330 Jun 2026 \u2192 `FY26`). It exposes `ordinal`, `yearSegment`, `label` (`FY<YY>`), and `elapsed` (whole fiscal years between two dates).\n\n**Behaviour changes:**\n1. **Membership identifier's year segment** (`OwnerMapper` + `LogOwnerAudit`) \u2014 `<customerCode>-M<YY>` now uses the fiscal-year two-digit year instead of the calendar year.\n2. **Tenure** (`MembershipLevel`) \u2014 the +3 points now trigger on at least one *elapsed fiscal year* rather than a >365-day window. A freshly created owner still has zero tenure (same fiscal year), preserving the \"fresh owner tops out at 5 points\" invariant.\n\n**New field:** `fiscalYear` added to the `Owner` schema in `openapi.yml` (so the generated `OwnerDto` gains it), mapped from the owner's persisted business-day-adjusted registration date.\n\nI derived `fiscalYear` (and the membership year segment) from `owner.getRegistrationDate()`, which `ApplyRegistrationDate` already stores business-day-adjusted \u2014 so the fiscal year is correctly computed from the adjusted date. I verified consistency in the run: an owner registered 2026-08-11 got `membershipNumber=...-M27` and would report `fiscalYear=FY27` (Aug 2026 falls in the fiscal year ending 2027).\n\nI also updated the affected OpenAPI descriptions (`membershipNumber`, `membershipPoints`) to match the new semantics.",
